// The reserved uid slot is RENAMED to `trace_id` by the event schema
// (event.dwschema). A Read is permitted only if the SAME user formerly
// logged in under a specific trace id, matched by a LITERAL on the renamed
// slot. The interpreter matches `trace_id` by descending the event's field
// tree (`field_path`) exactly like any other field — it has no special
// knowledge that this slot "used to be" `requestId`.
//
// A differential temporal engine must therefore serialize and read `trace_id`
// as an ordinary field, regardless of the fact that the default schema
// calls the uid slot `requestId`. A compiler that hardcodes the reserved
// slot names (or a positional args-array that reserves the last slot for
// "uid") mishandles the renamed slot.
//
// Controls:
//   trace_1: past Login with trace_id "tr-1" (matches the literal) -> the
//            current Read is PERMITTED.
//   trace_2: past Login with trace_id "tr-OTHER" (does not match) -> NOT
//            permitted (the literal genuinely constrains the match).
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user, trace_id: "tr-1" }
};
